            "text": "WN25-UR-000160 - The Windows Server 2025 \"Lock pages in memory\" user right must not be assigned to any groups or accounts."
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "family": "windows"
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "name": "platform",
                "namespace": "http://oval.mitre.org/XMLSchema/oval-definitions-5",
                "text": "Microsoft Windows Server 2025"
              }
            ],
            "name": "affected",
            "namespace": "http://oval.mitre.org/XMLSchema/oval-definitions-5"
          },
          {
            "name": "description",
            "namespace": "http://oval.mitre.org/XMLSchema/oval-definitions-5",
            "text": "Inappropriately granting user rights provides system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\n  The \"Lock pages in memory\" user right allows physical memory to be assigned to processes, which could cause performance issues or a denial of service.\n\n  Satisfies: SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125, SRG-OS-000433-GPOS-00193"
          }
        ],
        "name": "metadata",
        "namespace": "http://oval.mitre.org/XMLSchema/oval-definitions-5"
